  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=2x+y?$",
  "worked_solution": "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 2x+y & =c \\\\ y & =-2x+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $-2.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14247393/assets/ff1117065d7475786dd6c45f71f14d78b32cb3273123ced1adf5a67b750dacdd.png)",
